  "verbalization": "Xenognosin B is implicated in the interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a key component of the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2). This complex is known to regulate gene expression by methylating histone H3 lysine 27, and it is a well-established target of various small molecules. The evidence suggests that Xenognosin B acts as a modulator of this complex, with multiple compounds targeting the same pathway leading to the same downstream effect on SN12K1. The shared target of these compounds, SN12K1, indicates a potential mechanism of action involving the regulation of gene expression through the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Xenognosin B in modulating the activity of this complex, thereby influencing SN12K1. The evidence supports a mechanism where Xenognosin B may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex to affect SN12K1, potentially through the modulation of gene expression.",
